# Verdaccio 6.10.2 environment schema (@env-spec / varlock format).
#
# THIS FILE IS SHORT ON PURPOSE. Verdaccio is not an env-configured app. Its
# entire configuration surface is /verdaccio/conf/config.yaml (storage, auth,
# package ACLs, uplinks, the web UI, rate limits, TLS, notifications), and the
# handful of variables below are the only ones the code or the image's own
# entrypoint read at 6.10.2. Do not expect a variable for a config.yaml key:
# there isn't one, and inventing one silently does nothing. THE TEMPLATE SHIPS
# THAT config.yaml (see the security section below); edit it there, not here.
#
# There is also NO `${ENV}` interpolation in config.yaml at this version, a
# claim worth killing because it is widely repeated. @verdaccio/config 8.3.0's
# `parseConfigFile` is a plain `js-yaml.load` of the file with no substitution
# pass, so `secret: ${MY_SECRET}` is stored as the literal string. Exactly
# three env paths reach the config: `uplinks.<name>.auth.token_env: MY_VAR`
# (or `token_env: true`, meaning NPM_TOKEN), the http_proxy/https_proxy/
# no_proxy fallbacks, and VERDACCIO_STORAGE_PATH overriding `storage`.
#
# Source: grep of process.env across verdaccio v6.10.2's own src/ plus every
# @verdaccio/* runtime dependency it pins (config 8.3.0, url 13.1.3, signature
# 8.1.3, core 8.3.0, auth 8.1.3, middleware 8.1.3, local-storage-legacy
# 11.4.3, tarball 13.1.3, htpasswd/audit 13.1.3), cross-read against the
# image Dockerfile and docker-bin/uid_entrypoint.
#
# Two variables the docs list that the code does NOT read at 6.10.2, so they
# are deliberately absent: VERDACCIO_STORAGE_NAME (the db filename is the
# hardcoded constant `.verdaccio-db.json` in local-storage-legacy and
# @verdaccio/core; nothing looks the variable up) and
# EXPERIMENTAL_VERDACCIO_LOGGER_COLORS (still in the repo's
# docs/env.variables.md, gone from @verdaccio/logger 8.1.3 and from the
# website). PACKAGE_VERSION is likewise absent: vite replaces it at build.
#
# HOME / XDG_CONFIG_HOME / XDG_DATA_HOME / APPDATA appear in
# @verdaccio/config's config-path.ts but are dead in this image: the CMD
# always passes an explicit `--config /verdaccio/conf/config.yaml`, so the
# config-discovery path never runs.
#
# ─── SECURITY: the config this template ships, and what it changed ─────────
# This template does NOT let the image seed its own config. It ships
# config.yaml and binds it over /verdaccio/conf/config.yaml, because the image
# seed (@verdaccio/config's docker.yaml) is a demo config, not a private
# registry. Measured on 6.10.2 booted from that seed:
#
#   PUT /-/user/org.couchdb.user:mallory  ->  201 "user 'mallory' created"
#   GET /is-promise (no credentials)      ->  200
#
# That is `npm adduser` open to anyone who can reach the port. Both package
# patterns carry `publish: $authenticated`, so the account that call mints
# immediately satisfies publish AND unpublish on every package. The route is
# gated by nothing else: src/api/endpoint/api/user.ts calls `auth.add_user`
# behind only the rate limiter, `flags.createUser` is a web-UI flag that does
# not touch it, and verdaccio-htpasswd 13.1.3 defaults maxUsers to Infinity
# when `max_users` is absent, which upstream's file leaves absent.
#
# The shipped file changes exactly two things and keeps the rest of upstream's
# (storage paths, the npmjs uplink, audit middleware, logging):
#
#   auth.htpasswd.max_users: -1     PUT /-/user/... -> 409, verified
#   packages.*.access: $authenticated   anonymous GET -> 401, verified
#
# Consequences an operator has to know, all confirmed by running it:
#
#   * `npm adduser` AND `npm login` are closed for EVERYONE, existing users
#     included. The endpoint only takes its login branch when the request
#     already carries credentials, and Auth.add_user has no authenticate
#     fallback. Bootstrap the first account by appending to the htpasswd file
#     on the storage volume (the exact command is in config.yaml), then use
#     basic auth (`_auth` in .npmrc) or the token from the web UI login.
#   * The web UI's JWT is NOT an npm API token: putting it in `_authToken`
#     fails E401. Use `_auth`, or the token returned by
#     `PUT /-/user/...` sent WITH basic auth.
#   * `proxy: npmjs` is kept on BOTH patterns. '@*/*' matches every scoped
#     package, not just yours, so dropping it there would break @types/* and
#     every public scoped dependency.
#   * UPGRADING AN ALREADY-EXPOSED INSTANCE: `max_users: -1` closes new
#     registrations, it does not revoke old ones. Accounts registered while
#     the permissive default was live persist in /verdaccio/storage/htpasswd
#     (that volume is deliberately preserved) and keep authenticating. Audit
#     that file.
#   * Password floor stays upstream's 3 characters
#     (`server.passwordValidationRegex`, /.{3}$/).

# @defaultSensitive=false @defaultRequired=infer
# @docs("Environment Variables", https://verdaccio.org/docs/env)
# ---

# ─── Container listener ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Port Verdaccio listens on inside the container. NOT read by Verdaccio's own
# code: the image bakes it to 4873 and its CMD interpolates it into
# `verdaccio --listen $VERDACCIO_PROTOCOL://$VERDACCIO_ADDRESS:$VERDACCIO_PORT`
# via /bin/sh. The compose exposes container port 4873 with no override, so
# this is that port's twin: change one without the other and routing breaks.
# @type=port
# @docs("Docker", https://verdaccio.org/docs/docker)
VERDACCIO_PORT=4873

# Scheme in the same CMD-built `--listen` argument. `https` makes Verdaccio
# terminate TLS ITSELF, which additionally requires an `https:` block in
# config.yaml with `key` and `cert` paths mounted into the container; without
# it the process exits at boot. Behind the platform edge, leave it `http`.
# @type=enum(http, https)
# @docs("Set up the SSL Certificates", https://verdaccio.org/docs/ssl)
VERDACCIO_PROTOCOL=http

# Bind address in the same `--listen` argument. The image default is
# `0.0.0.0` on the 6.x line (it becomes `[::]` in the next major), which is
# what a container network needs. Binding 127.0.0.1 makes the service
# unreachable from outside the container.
VERDACCIO_ADDRESS=0.0.0.0

# Read by the image's `uid_entrypoint`, not by Verdaccio. When the container
# is started under an arbitrary UID (OpenShift-style) that has no /etc/passwd
# entry, the entrypoint appends one under this name so `whoami` resolves.
VERDACCIO_USER_NAME=verdaccio

# Graceful shutdown. Compared as the exact STRING "true" in
# src/lib/bootstrap.ts; "1", "yes" or "TRUE" do nothing. When on, SIGINT /
# SIGTERM / SIGHUP close the HTTP server and drain in-flight requests before
# exiting instead of dying immediately. Off by default on 6.x; the next major
# removes the variable and always shuts down gracefully.
# @type=enum(true)
VERDACCIO_HANDLE_KILL_SIGNALS=

# ─── Public URL and reverse proxying ───────────────────────────────────────

# THE variable to get right on a proxied registry. @verdaccio/url 13.1.3
# `getPublicUrl` prefers it over the request's Host and X-Forwarded-Proto
# headers, and its result is what rewrites every `dist.tarball` URL in the
# metadata a client receives. Wrong, and `npm install` fetches metadata fine
# and then fails on tarballs pointing at an internal name.
#
# Two traps. (1) It is validated with `new URL()` and SILENTLY IGNORED if it
# does not parse with an http/https scheme, so a bare `npm.example.com`
# produces no error, it just falls back to the Host header. Include the
# scheme. (2) If `url_prefix` is set in config.yaml it is resolved as an
# absolute path against this value, so any path component here is DISCARDED:
# `https://x.org/first` + `url_prefix: /second` yields `https://x.org/second/`.
# Leave empty to derive the URL from Host + X-Forwarded-Proto, which is
# correct behind a proxy that sets both.
# @type=url
# @docs("Reverse Proxy Setup", https://verdaccio.org/docs/reverse-proxy)
VERDACCIO_PUBLIC_URL=

# Name of the header Verdaccio reads the client-side scheme from when
# VERDACCIO_PUBLIC_URL is empty. Defaults to `X-Forwarded-Proto`; set it only
# for an edge that uses a different one (e.g. `CloudFront-Forwarded-Proto`).
# Lowercased before lookup, so case here does not matter.
VERDACCIO_FORWARDED_PROTO=

# ─── Storage ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Overrides config.yaml's `storage` key (@verdaccio/config Config constructor
# reads it first). The shipped config.yaml points storage at
# /verdaccio/storage/data, and the compose mounts a volume at
# /verdaccio/storage, which also covers the htpasswd file and
# .verdaccio-db.json. Repointing this outside /verdaccio/storage moves the
# packages off the persistent volume; they vanish on redeploy.
# @docs("Configuration File", https://verdaccio.org/docs/configuration)
VERDACCIO_STORAGE_PATH=

# ─── Legacy (pre-JWT) token encryption ─────────────────────────────────────

# Overrides the key used to encrypt/decrypt LEGACY npm bearer tokens
# (@verdaccio/signature). It is not storage encryption. By default those
# tokens use the server secret that Verdaccio generates and persists in
# .verdaccio-db.json; setting this pins them to a key you control, which is
# how you keep old tokens valid across a secret rotation. Must be EXACTLY 32
# characters. aesEncrypt throws "Invalid secret key length" otherwise, and
# every legacy-token login fails.
# @sensitive
# @type=string(matches=/^.{32}$/)
VERDACCIO_LEGACY_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# Cipher for those same legacy tokens; any name from `crypto.getCiphers()` in
# the container's Node build. Only change it to match tokens minted elsewhere.
# Changing it on a live registry invalidates every legacy token in the wild.
VERDACCIO_LEGACY_ALGORITHM=aes-256-ctr

# ─── Uplinks ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Fallback credential for an uplink. src/lib/up-storage.ts uses it whenever an
# uplink declares an `auth:` block without an inline `token`, and explicitly
# when that block says `token_env: true`. Only meaningful if you add an
# authenticated uplink (a private npm org, an Artifactory). The shipped
# config.yaml's single `npmjs` uplink is anonymous and ignores this. Point
# individual uplinks at differently-named variables with
# `token_env: MY_OTHER_VAR` instead of sharing one token.
# @sensitive
# @docs("Uplinks", https://verdaccio.org/docs/uplinks)
NPM_TOKEN=

# ─── Outbound proxy ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Standard proxy variables for Verdaccio's own outbound fetches to uplinks.
# @verdaccio/config copies them onto the config object ONLY if the same key is
# absent from config.yaml, checking the lowercase name first and the uppercase
# one second, so a `http_proxy:` line in config.yaml wins over both, and
# these do nothing if it is present.
# @docs("Configuration File", https://verdaccio.org/docs/configuration)
http_proxy=
HTTP_PROXY=
https_proxy=
HTTPS_PROXY=
# Comma-separated hosts that bypass the proxy, e.g. "localhost,127.0.0.1".
no_proxy=
NO_PROXY=
